    "long_instructions": "# Modify: Debug\r\n\r\nYour Task: Another crew wrote this program to paint the path in front of the food truck, but their checks do the opposite of what they should. Find the bug and fix it, so the Painter paints all four squares and turns to face the truck.\r\n\r\nDo This:\r\n\r\n1. Run the code and read the error message.\r\n2. Look at where the Painter stopped and which squares got painted.\r\n3. Trace the first two checks. Is `can_move()` True or False each time? Which branch ran, and is that the right thing for the Painter to do?\r\n4. Fix the bug. There is more than one way to fix it.\r\n5. Run again to check your fix, then use Validate.",
    "start_sources": {
      "files": {
        "0": {
          "id": "0",
          "name": "main.py",
          "contents": "from neighborhood import *\n\n# Painter setup: these lines restock the Painter and move it to the start of the path.\nmove()\ntake_paint()\ntake_paint()\ntake_paint()\ntake_paint()\nmove()\nturn_left()\nturn_left()\nturn_left()\nmove()\nturn_left()\n\n# Your code goes below\n# Each square: paint it, then check whether the Painter can move.\n\n# Square 1\npaint(\"white\")\nif can_move():\n    turn_left()\n    turn_left()\n    turn_left()\nelse:\n    move()\n\n# Square 2\npaint(\"white\")\nif can_move():\n    turn_left()\n    turn_left()\n    turn_left()\nelse:\n    move()\n\n# Square 3\npaint(\"white\")\nif can_move():\n    turn_left()\n    turn_left()\n    turn_left()\nelse:\n    move()\n\n# Square 4\npaint(\"white\")\nif can_move():\n    turn_left()\n    turn_left()\n    turn_left()\nelse:\n    move()",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": false
        }
